## Fix "already exists" false positive when editing relationship direction

Context: After the live-canvas-refresh fix (`loadOntologyIntoDesigner` at the end
of `saveSharedRelationship`), the call fires `scheduleAutoSave()` via the OntoViz
`onChange` callback. That auto-save runs `syncDesignToOntology` 500 ms later, which
rewrites `OntologyState.config.properties` (DataType properties first, ObjectProperties
after), changing the array indices. If the user re-opens the same panel within those
500 ms, `sharedPanelEditIndex` no longer matches the relationship's new position, and
the index-based duplicate check finds the relationship at a different index → false
positive "A relationship named … already exists".  The same race existed for entities.

Changes:

1. src/front/static/ontology/js/ontology-shared-panels.js
   - `saveSharedRelationship()`: duplicate check now short-circuits to `false` when
     `name === sharedPanelOriginalName && sharedPanelEditIndex >= 0` (name-unchanged
     edit such as a direction change).  The index-based path is only reached for new
     relationships or renames, where an index collision is an actual duplicate.
   - `saveSharedEntity()`: same fix applied for entity edits (e.g. icon, parent,
     description changes that do not rename the entity).

Modified files:
- src/front/static/ontology/js/ontology-shared-panels.js

Test result: `uv run --frozen pytest -q -m "not scenario"` → 4965 passed,
281 skipped, 6 deselected, 1 xfailed.

