## Fix "Loading mapping design…" spinner that never ended

Context: The mapping design section showed a persistent loading spinner because
`initMappingDesigner()` awaited `loadSchemaDrift()` inside a `Promise.all`.
`/mapping/schema-drift` runs a live warehouse query and takes ~19 s; the spinner
blocked for the entire duration. The function's own comment already documented
that schema-drift is "advisory only — a failure leaves the designer working with
no drift markers," so blocking the spinner on it was incorrect.

Changes:

1. src/front/static/mapping/js/mapping-design.js (line ~169)
   Replaced `await Promise.all([loadMapLayout(), loadSchemaDrift()])` with
   `await loadMapLayout()` (fast, session-local) followed by
   `loadSchemaDrift().then(() => { if (mappingMapInitialized) initMappingDesigner(); }).catch(() => {})`.
   Schema-drift now fires in the background; when it resolves, the designer
   silently re-renders to pick up any drift markers on nodes and panels.

2. tests/units/front/test_schema_drift_ui.py
   Updated `test_fetched_in_parallel_with_the_map_layout` (renamed to
   `test_fetched_without_blocking_the_spinner`) to assert the new pattern:
   schema-drift is NOT in the blocking await path, fires via `.then()`, and
   `loadMapLayout()` is still awaited.

