## Fix relationship direction arrow not updating in the D3 ontology map (section=map)

Context: When the user edits a relationship's direction in the right-hand panel while
on the `map` section (D3 force-directed graph), the arrow in the graph did not flip.
The D3 map always rendered arrows via the CSS `marker-end: url(#map-arrow)` rule applied
to every `.map-link` element; there was no mechanism to reflect the `direction` property
from the link data. Three changes are needed: (1) a `map-arrow-start` SVG marker that
points in the reverse direction (using `orient="auto-start-reverse"`), (2) the CSS class
`reverse` that overrides `marker-end: none` and activates `marker-start`, and (3) a
`refreshMapLinkDirection(name, direction)` function that flips the class on the live DOM
element without a full map reload.

Changes:

1. src/front/static/ontology/js/ontology-map.js
   - Added `map-arrow-start` SVG marker to `<defs>` in `initOntologyMap`, using
     `orient="auto-start-reverse"` so it points backward along the path (toward source).
   - Changed `.attr('class', 'map-link')` to `.attr('class', d => ...)` so links with
     `direction === 'reverse'` are initialised with the `reverse` CSS class.
   - Added `refreshMapLinkDirection(name, direction)` at module level: updates the live
     `ontologyMapLinks` data and toggles the `reverse` class on the matching SVG `path`
     via a D3 selection. Exposed as `window.refreshMapLinkDirection`.

2. src/front/static/ontology/css/ontology-map.css
   Added `.map-link.reverse { marker-end: none; marker-start: url(#map-arrow-start); }`
   so the CSS handles the marker swap when the `reverse` class is toggled.

3. src/front/static/ontology/js/ontology-shared-panels.js
   `saveSharedRelationship()`: added a call to `refreshMapLinkDirection(lookupName, direction)`
   alongside the existing `refreshRelationshipInDesigner` call. Both are guarded by
   `typeof ... === 'function'` so they are no-ops when the respective view was never opened.

