## Fix spurious "Source schema changed" warnings in the Mapping Designer

Context: Opening an entity or relationship panel in the Mapping Designer intermittently
showed a schema-drift banner listing *every* bound column ("9 mapped column(s) no longer
exist upstream: ID, Label, lastname, …") for mappings that were perfectly valid. Two
independent defects were involved.

The drift banner is fed by `GET /mapping/schema-drift`, which compares the columns bound
by a mapping against the physical schema returned by `DESCRIBE`. Designer- and
auto-assignment-generated mappings bind to the *SELECT projection* of their SQL query —
i.e. aliases such as `AS ID` / `AS Label` / lowercase attribute aliases — which by design
never match the base table's column names, so every bound column was flagged as dropped.
`run_diagnostics()` already guarded against this (`if result["available_columns"] is
None`), but `get_schema_drift()` did not. The warnings looked transient because the
designer only paints them once the (slow) warehouse query returns; a page refresh reset
the state until the next fetch completed.

The second defect made the first far more visible: `initMappingDesigner()` re-rendered
itself from the `loadSchemaDrift().then(...)` callback, and that re-render fired a new
drift fetch — an unbounded loop re-running N `DESCRIBE` statements against the warehouse
for as long as the designer stayed open.

Changes:

1. src/back/objects/mapping/Mapping.py
   - Added `_binds_to_sql_projection()`: `True` when a mapping's `sql_query` has a
     readable SELECT list (via `DigitalTwin._extract_select_columns`). `SELECT *` and
     unparseable clauses return `False`, where the table schema is still the right
     comparison.
   - `_entity_drift_checks()` / `_relationship_drift_checks()` now return `[]` for such
     mappings, so the guard lives in one place instead of being re-implemented by each
     caller.
   - `run_diagnostics()`: dropped the duplicated `available_columns is None` conditions —
     the drift helpers now self-guard.
   - `get_schema_drift()`: returns early (no warehouse round-trips at all) when every
     active mapping binds to its own projection.

2. src/front/static/mapping/js/mapping-design.js
   - Added the `mappingDriftLoaded` flag, set at the end of `loadSchemaDrift()`; the
     drift fetch in `initMappingDesigner()` is now guarded by it, breaking the
     render → fetch → render loop.
   - `refreshMappingDesign()` clears the flag so an explicit refresh after a mapping
     change still re-checks drift exactly once.

3. tests/units/mapping/test_schema_drift.py
   - New cases: aliased entity SQL reports no drift; a projection-only mapping performs
     zero `get_table_columns` calls; `SELECT *` mappings are still checked; aliased
     relationship SQL reports no drift.

Modified files:
- src/back/objects/mapping/Mapping.py
- src/front/static/mapping/js/mapping-design.js
- tests/units/mapping/test_schema_drift.py

