## Honour relationship direction in the Mapping Designer canvas

Context: Reverse relationships were drawn with the arrowhead at the target end in the
Mapping Designer, so the canvas contradicted both the Ontology Designer and the generated
triples. `direction: 'reverse'` means the relationship is emitted target → source
(`R2RMLGenerator._generate_relationship` swaps the two sides), and the Ontology map already
renders that with a start-placed marker. The Mapping designer carried `direction` on every
link datum but never used it: no `reverse` class, no start marker.

Changes:

1. src/front/static/mapping/js/mapping-design.js
   - Added three start-arrow markers — `mapping-arrow-start-mapped` (green),
     `-unmapped` (red), `-excluded` (grey) — with `orient='auto-start-reverse'`, mirroring
     `map-arrow-start` in ontology-map.js but keeping the designer's per-state colours.
   - Relationship link elements now append a `reverse` class when
     `d.direction === 'reverse'`, additive to the existing mapped/unmapped/excluded class.

2. src/front/static/mapping/css/mapping-design.css
   - Added `.mapping-map-link.reverse.{mapped,unmapped,excluded}` rules that clear
     `marker-end` and set the matching `marker-start`. The excluded variant repeats
     `!important` because the base `.excluded` rule sets its marker that way.

3. tests/units/front/test_mapping_link_direction.py (new)
   - Contract tests: one start marker per link state, markers are `auto-start-reverse`,
     the `reverse` class is additive to the state class, each CSS rule swaps
     `marker-end` for `marker-start`, and the ontology-map contract still holds.

